    "These are the supplied sheet\u2019s judgment brackets, not modeled odds or verified election calls. Candidate names and timings are transcribed from the sheet; use linked reporting to verify updates.",
    "A blue wave should be clear by 9pm according to the sheet. Tight at 11pm suggests a long night or week; this app does not infer chamber control from a partial watchlist.",
    "Senate: the sheet says Democrats need a net gain of 4 seats for control. House: 218 is a majority. These are reference scenarios, not totals calculated from this watchlist.",
    "Margins use Democrat minus Republican percentage points (Osborn minus Ricketts in Nebraska). Literal rounded chart bands leave some fractional margins between bands; the tracker leaves those unclassified.",
    "Redrawn House seats: an incumbent behind their 2024 county vote pace may be saved by late votes. The sheet marks these with a star.",
    "Dashed House guardrails: Florida redraw targets FL-09, FL-14, FL-22, FL-25 (GOP 4 for 4); Texas targets TX-09, TX-28, TX-32, TX-34, TX-35 (GOP 4+ of 5; the sheet quotes \u201clucky to get three\u201d); PA-07 and PA-10 are rated Lean D (GOP 2 for 2).",
